WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.862 --> 00:00:07.862
Once your school gives you a seat, the next job is to build your lesson plan library. This video shows you how.

2
00:00:08.364 --> 00:00:24.694
On My Licenses, a green banner says you can pick up to forty plans. You can add more any time. If you change your mind, you can swap a plan out a limited number of times. So choose the ones you really plan to teach. Select Browse Lesson Plans.

3
00:00:25.196 --> 00:00:31.136
This is the full catalogue. The counter at the top shows how many plans you've added, out of your limit.

4
00:00:31.637 --> 00:00:37.187
To narrow the list, choose a grade level, pick a series, or type in the search box.

5
00:00:42.182 --> 00:00:45.752
When you find a lesson you want, select Add to Library.

6
00:00:46.255 --> 00:01:00.345
You'll see a short confirmation. If you take a plan out later, that costs one of your swaps, and the box tells you how many you have left. If you're not sure, select Cancel. Otherwise, select Add to My Library.

7
00:01:00.847 --> 00:01:06.257
The lesson is marked Added, and the counter goes up by one. Add the rest the same way.

8
00:01:06.759 --> 00:01:15.159
Select My Lesson Plans to see your library. Your plans are here, and you can search them, or select View Lesson to open one.

9
00:01:15.661 --> 00:01:25.081
Changed your mind about a plan? Select Swap or remove on its card. Either one uses a swap, and the badge at the top shows how many you have left.

10
00:01:25.582 --> 00:01:34.982
Need more later? Select Add Plans. If your license is a trial, your limit can be lower than forty, and the counter at the top always shows it.
